  "title": "Weekly California Capacity Report, assembled and mailed by hand",
  "task_class": "recurring_report",
  "label_mechanical": "Recurring report production and distribution: distribute california / capacity / report",
  "narrative": {
    "what_happens": "Each week one person on the Transwestern commercial side compiles a California capacity summary and mails it to a standing distribution list. The body follows the same template every time: average Transwestern deliveries to California, San Juan lateral throughput, El Paso deliveries broken out by delivery point, and posted Gas Daily prices. The figures are pulled together from separate sources \u2014 spreadsheets and pipeline website postings appear alongside the mail itself \u2014 and then typed or pasted into the message rather than generated by a system. The output is the email itself; the thread ends when it is sent, with no confirmations or replies visible in the cluster.",
    "where_it_stalls": "The stall is not waiting on anyone \u2014 no waiting or deadline signals appear at all. It is that nearly every instance carries a manual-transfer signal: the same numbers are re-keyed out of spreadsheets and pipeline postings into a fresh email week after week, by a single sender with no visible backup. The cost of that hand assembly shows in the one correction instance, where the report went out with the wrong effective week and had to be re-sent (\"Sorry, the effective date for this new report is 01/07-01/11\") \u2014 a header field nobody re-derived from the underlying data.",
    "why_it_recurs": "The report is on a fixed weekly cadence to a fixed distribution list, and the source figures live in spreadsheets and pipeline postings that do not feed the mail directly, so the assembly is repeated from scratch each week.",
    "automation_opportunity": "A scheduled job that reads the delivery and throughput figures and the posted Gas Daily prices from their sources, renders them into the existing fixed template with the week's date range derived from the run date, and mails it to the standing list \u2014 leaving the sender only to review and release it.",
    "coherence": "tight"
  },
